 {"id":"fabro-09ea","title":"engine: per-automation on_overlap policy — skip scheduled fires while a previous run is non-terminal","status":"closed","type":"feature","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-02T19:05:22.328Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-04T07:16:08.741Z","description":"STATUS: code complete, tested, pushed (1bf515770); DEPLOY PENDING — deliberately withheld while revisor run 01M1HKRE686W833SE86D8WD319 is active (user directive 2026-09-02). Deploy with `just up` once the run is terminal, then verify migration 2026090201 applied on production.\n\nLANDED: AutomationOverlapPolicy (fire|skip) through model/store/migration/OpenAPI/TS; scheduler skip guard (INFO, no run, no last_error; overlap-check failure also skips); manual API triggers unconditional. Tests: column round-trip, scheduler skip proof + default-fire control. ADR-0011 amendment recorded (gates wait indefinitely; overlap prevention replaces timeouts; timeout stays the per-node opt-in). automations.mdx docs.\n\nOriginal design: per-automation on_overlap for scheduled fires — skip while a previous run of the same automation is non-terminal (incl. gate-blocked, which can wait indefinitely). Known accepted window: terminal previous run with still-open PR not covered (auto-merge closes in seconds).","closedAt":"2026-09-04T07:16:08.741Z"}
 {"id":"fabro-18a5","title":"Terminal soft-exit edges classify runs as succeeded, blocking resume in CLI and web UI","status":"closed","type":"bug","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T05:48:55.539Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-04T21:37:58.600Z","description":"\n\nFIX LANDED 2026-09-04 (33a856869, deployed same day via just up rebuild): apply_soft_exit_downgrade in pipeline/finalize.rs mirrors the boundary upgrade in reverse — a success-shaped outcome routed through a kind=\"deadlock\"/\"soft\" exit edge becomes a failed terminal with FailureReason::Deadlock/SoftStop, the explicit failure detail lands in the persisted conclusion (resume unblocked), and publish gets its own exit-kind eligibility check (publish runs before finalize). Unit + pipeline e2e tests: soft_exit_downgrade_converts_green_terminal_to_failed, deadlock_exit_with_green_outcome_fails_instead_of_publishing. Live motivation: run 01M1PVMS7B6N39MG0041C5F7P6 (pre-fix binary) classified a closeout-failure soft exit as succeeded(completed) and opened PR #14-class artifact PR #18; with the rebuilt binary the re-run 01M1Q4P92K5RX8XX990BEB130Y completed naturally (closeout green) — the soft path is covered by tests, no live soft exit forced.","labels":["needs-triage"],"closedAt":"2026-09-04T21:37:58.341Z"}
 {"id":"fabro-83af","title":"Graph-level retry policy with backoff config and node-level override for stage retries","status":"open","type":"feature","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T05:49:01.421Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T13:23:27.573Z","description":"Stage retries today (lib/components/fabro-workflow/src/retry.rs) support node attributes 'retry_policy' (presets: none/standard/aggressive/linear/patient) and 'max_retries', plus a single graph attribute 'default_max_retries' that sets only the attempt count. The backoff shape is hardcoded (initial 5s, factor 2.0, cap 60s, jitter) and presets can only be selected per node.\n\nGap: transient provider errors (e.g. zai 429 rate limits) can hit ANY LLM node in a workflow, so the retry default belongs at workflow level. Today every LLM node repeats 'retry_policy=standard' manually (see revisor graph nodes select/analyze/file in run 01M1HKRE686W833SE86D8WD319); forgetting one node silently leaves it without retries.\n\nDemand: declare a retry policy once at graph level (preset name, and optionally explicit backoff attributes initial_delay/factor/max_delay/jitter), applying to all nodes. Node attributes override the workflow default for special cases. Precedence: node retry_policy > node max_retries > graph retry_policy/backoff > graph default_max_retries > none. Exponential backoff with jitter already exists (fabro_util::backoff) and should stay the default shape.","labels":["needs-triage"],"assignee":"fabro"}
-{"id":"fabro-a3d8","title":"Long-window rate limits defeat count-based retries: honor provider reset times or park-and-resume","status":"in_progress","type":"feature","priority":0,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T05:49:08.872Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-11T22:35:58.178Z","description":"Evidence: run 01M1HKRE686W833SE86D8WD319 burned its full stage retry budget (5 attempts, exponential backoff 5s..40s, ~2 min total) against a zai 429 whose usage window reset only hours later ('Usage limit reached for 5 hour. Your limit will reset at 2026-09-03 05:35:16'). The provider sent retry_after=null; the reset timestamp exists only inside the error message text. Three nested retry layers (agent.llm.retry x3, stage retries x5) all exhaust quickly against a multi-hour window, then the run soft-exits.\n\nCount-based exponential backoff cannot bridge multi-hour provider windows: the delays are far too short and the attempt count exhausts within minutes while the limit stays.\n\nFix directions to evaluate: (1) parse provider reset/retry-after hints (header AND message text) and cap or extend retry delays accordingly; (2) a wall-clock retry budget option (retry until T) instead of/in addition to attempt counts; (3) park-and-resume semantics: on a long-window 429, park the run in a resumable state with a scheduled wake-up instead of exhausting retries and exiting. Related: fabro-18a5 (soft-exit runs cannot be resumed), fabro-83af (graph-level retry defaults).\n\nEVIDENCE 2026-09-11 (integrate batch, recurrence confirmed same day): midday conductor passes on the second machine died on ZAI 5h-usage-limit 429s (conductor 01M269AXA and 01M26H7ZCA46 at 12:00/12:30 Berlin; merge child 01M27V6 at 11:27 — handoff fabro-91bf). None were resumable after the quota reset: recovery required manual new passes (13:20 API trigger) and a 2h salvage for merge child 01M2837. Code status at 23:5x Berlin: fabro-llm default_retry_policy = 3 attempts with backoff capped at 5s (client.rs); 429 maps to ErrorKind::RateLimit and Retry-After is parsed (gateway.rs), but retry exhaustion fails the run hard (workflow_error) — no park. Engine resume primitive exists (operations/resume.rs, POST /api/v1/runs/{id}/start {\"resume\":true}) but has the documented re-park trap when a routing decision already committed (see fabro-7627 engine part), and nothing triggers it on provider recovery. Priority raised P2->P1 by user decision 2026-09-11 ~23:59 Berlin; user ordering: this seed first, then fabro-7627 (manual resume UI+rewind). PRIORITY NOTE: raised P1->P0 by user decision 2026-09-12 00:29 Berlin to jump the develop queue — recurring unrecoverable outage class with same-day recurrence; user ordering: this seed next, then fabro-7627 (dep edge already in place).","labels":["needs-triage"],"assignee":"fabro","blocks":["fabro-7627"]}
