d Retry-After is parsed (gateway.rs), but retry exhaustion fails the run hard (workflow_error) — no park. Engine resume primitive exists (operations/resume.rs, POST /api/v1/runs/{id}/start {\"resume\":true}) but has the documented re-park trap when a routing decision already committed (see fabro-7627 engine part), and nothing triggers it on provider recovery. Priority raised P2->P1 by user decision 2026-09-11 ~23:59 Berlin; user ordering: this seed first, then fabro-7627 (manual resume UI+rewind). PRIORITY NOTE: raised P1->P0 by user decision 2026-09-12 00:29 Berlin to jump the develop queue — recurring unrecoverable outage class with same-day recurrence; user ordering: this seed next, then fabro-7627 (dep edge already in place).","labels":["needs-triage"],"assignee":"fabro","blocks":["fabro-7627"],"closedAt":"2026-09-11T23:21:22.354Z"}
 {"id":"fabro-b440","title":"rewind/fork UX: starting a fork with checkpoints ends terminal failed(terminated) — queue forks in resume mode or auto-switch","status":"open","type":"bug","priority":3,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T06:03:02.286Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T13:23:27.778Z","description":"Scope NARROWED 2026-09-03 after verification on merged v0.345.0-nightly.0 (merge 6530c724f): upstream PR #838 fixed the crash-loop half — see VERIFIED below. What remains is fix direction (1): the happy path. `fabro rewind`/`fabro fork` produce a fork that CARRIES checkpoint history, but `fabro start <fork>` queues Start mode, hits the checkpoint precondition, and the fork ends terminal failed(terminated) within seconds. The rewind output already prints the correct recovery hint (\"To resume: fabro resume <fork-id>\"), so the remaining work is UX: queue forks in Resume mode by default (or have start auto-detect checkpoint history and switch), so users do not have to know the mode rule. Fix direction (3) (respawn backoff) is obsolete — no respawn happens anymore.\n\nOriginal report: after 'fabro rewind 01M1HKRE686W833SE86D8WD319 @41' (fork to 01M1JX979PTSZRZ10ZCTMJA34E), 'fabro start <new-run>' produced an infinite worker crash loop: every worker invocation died with 'Precondition failed: checkpoint already exists in the run store — did you mean to resume?' and the scheduler respawned it ~10x/second for minutes. Root cause: forked runs carry checkpoint history; queue_run_start (lib/apps/fabro-server/src/server/handler/lifecycle.rs) selects RunExecutionMode::Start for non-resume starts; operations::start refuses runs with existing checkpoints; the worker-exit failure event was rejected ('invalid status transition: runnable -> failed(terminated)') so the run stayed Runnable and spawn_scheduler retried forever. Correct recovery was 'fabro resume <fork-id>' (mode Resume), which worked.\n\nVERIFIED 2026-09-03 on v0.345.0-nightly.0 (server built from merge 6530c724f): reproduced the exact scenario — unarchived 01M1HKRE686W833SE86D8WD319, `fabro rewind ... @41` -> fork 01M1MG3JYMZ8DJW0G09QXKEH0Z, `fabro start` -> ONE worker invocation, worker stderr shows the precondition failure, run persists as terminal failed(terminated) (~4s from start to terminal; server log shows a single worker control-stream, zero respawns; second start attempt correctly rejected 409 'status is failed(terminated), expected submitted'). Both test runs re-archived afterwards.","labels":["needs-triage"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-8fb5","title":"Designed loops exhaust per-node max_visits and fail as workflow_error 'stuck in a cycle'","status":"open","type":"bug","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T06:03:20.266Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T13:23:27.880Z","description":"Evidence: revisor run 01M1JXPAABBQ3TM3DJ2DQ1VZDW (forked from 01M1HKRE686W833SE86D8WD319 at checkpoint @41) resumed cleanly, ran select@11 successfully (selected target 01M11P68SHFS165HP9ATK6094V), then terminated as failed/workflow_error: 'node \"analyze\" visited 10 times (node limit 10); run is stuck in a cycle'. The original run would have hit the same wall one stage later even without the zai 429 — the budget was already spent after 10 completed revision cycles.\n\nProblems: (1) the revisor graph (digraph Revisor) is a designed loop with a natural end ('Nothing to revise' edge), but per-node max_visits (analyze=10, file=10, select=15) turns a healthy, still-productive loop into a hard workflow_error once the budget is gone and backlog remains — 'stuck in a cycle' is misleading for a loop that is making progress each visit; (2) node visit counts persist across fork/resume, so forking a long-running loop near its budget cannot continue it at all — the fork burns a cycle and dies; (3) there is no graceful 'budget exhausted, park and re-enter next pass' terminal state distinct from an error.\n\nFix directions: distinguish progress-making loops from true cycles (e.g. only fail as stuck-in-cycle when a node repeats without forward state change / same failure signature), or add a designed 'budget exhausted' exit kind (soft/boundary) so loops can park resumably, and/or revisit the revisor graph's per-node caps (graph max_node_visits=30 already bounds the run).","labels":["needs-triage"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-9588","title":"Per-node skills and memory scoping for agent stages","status":"open","type":"feature","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T17:30:25.335Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T13:23:27.980Z","description":"Evidence: revisor run 01M1HKRE686W833SE86D8WD319 — every agent stage carries ~50 skill descriptions (~1.5k tokens) plus AGENTS.md memory (5.3KB) in its system prompt, regardless of need. Validation pass 01M1M568F5BZ9F17T3SFGRDCZ3 (2026-09-03) proved node attribute project_memory=false is INERT for agent nodes: AgentSession::initialize (lib/components/fabro-agent/src/session.rs ~line 625) calls discover_memory unconditionally; project_memory only gates the older prompt-handler path (lib/components/fabro-workflow/src/handler/prompt.rs line 68). select/analyze still loaded AGENTS.md (5307 bytes, budget 32768) with the attribute set.\n\nDemand: thread per-node scoping into the AGENT session path, not just the prompt handler. Cover BOTH: (a) memory — honor project_memory=false (or a dedicated memory=false) in AgentSession::initialize/AgentConfig; (b) skills — a per-node attribute (skills=false or skills=<dir>) to disable or scope skill discovery (AgentSession config already has skill_dirs, node-level override is missing). Both analogous to fs_hide/fabro_tools. Benefits every tool-light workflow stage.","labels":["needs-triage"],"assignee":"fabro"}
